## Frame ownership and dispatch

Steady delivery makes one owned-frame allocation. The same check exercises the
borrowed `FrameView` projection and records model struct sizes.

```=html
<!-- bench:frame-view GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<table>
<tr><th>metric</th><th>value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Allocations per delivered turn</td><td>1 (gated <code>== 1</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frame-view projections exercised</td><td>1,000,000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Argument / Message struct bytes</td><td>40 / 224</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reference / Resolution struct bytes</td><td>32 / 48</td></tr>
</table>
```

## Encrypted transport round-trip

`bench-iroh` times one full OCapN `greet` round-trip on loopback over
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh'))'s keyed QUIC and over cleartext TCP as a
baseline.

The first charts keep one call in flight. iroh's QUIC sidecar runs on another
runtime, so serial calls pay a cross-thread wake; the benchmark does not
separate that cost from encryption. The third chart overlaps sixteen iroh
connections on one readiness loop. Both bars there are iroh. Loopback removes
propagation delay and packet loss, so none of these values is field latency.

```=html
<!-- bench:iroh GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
