<tr><td>registry</td><td>0.71</td><td>0.33</td><td>0.32</td><td>1,198</td><td>3,011</td><td>3,004</td></tr>
<tr><td>mint</td><td>0.68</td><td>0.33</td><td>0.33</td><td>1,216</td><td>2,445</td><td>2,676</td></tr>
<tr><td>taskboard</td><td>1.46</td><td>0.68</td><td>0.65</td><td>564</td><td>1,504</td><td>1,446</td></tr>
</table>
```

## Per-language consumer cost, not a substrate comparison

One native Zig host stays fixed while the client changes. Each row includes a
runtime, binding, application, and garbage collector; it is not a language
race. Goblins is an outside CapTP peer, not another pancake binding. Method
details are in the
[bench README](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/bench/langs/README.md).

